  "cues": [
   [
    0.091,
    "There's a short way to write these sets, called interval notation."
   ],
   [
    3.984,
    "A square bracket means the endpoint is included, like a closed circle."
   ],
   [
    8.906,
    "A round parenthesis means it is not included, like an open circle."
   ],
   [
    13.685,
    "So negative three is less than or equal to x, which is less than two, is written square bracket negative three, comma, two, round parenthesis."
   ],
   [
    25.0,
    "A ray that never ends uses the infinity symbol, always with a round parenthesis, because infinity is not a number you can reach: x at least negative three is square bracket negative three, comma, infinity."
   ],
   [
    39.076,
    "All real numbers are negative infinity to infinity, and no solution is the empty set."
   ]
  ]
 },
